  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An alternative lexical label for a resource.</skos:definition>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">Acronyms, abbreviations, spelling variants, and irregular plural/singular forms may be included among the alternative labels for a concept. Mis-spelled terms are normally included as hidden labels (see skos:hiddenLabel).</skos:example>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The range of skos:altLabel is the class of RDF plain literals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">skos:prefLabel, skos:altLabel and skos:hiddenLabel are pairwise disjoint properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">alternative label</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/sulo/Capability">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Capability</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">the capability to fly, the capabilty to reduce the activation energy of a chemical reaction, the capability to reason</skos:example>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A capability is a feature that describes what an entity is able to do, under some set of circumstances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/sulo/Feature"/>
    <rdfs:label>capability</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Plan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Plan</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <prov:category>expanded</prov:category>
    <prov:category>qualified</prov:category>
    <prov:dm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-dm-20130430/#term-Association</prov:dm>
    <prov:n rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-n-20130430/#expression-Association</prov:n>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">There exist no prescriptive requirement on the nature of plans, their representation, the actions or steps they consist of, or their intended goals. Since plans may evolve over time, it may become necessary to track their provenance, so plans themselves are entities. Representing the plan explicitly in the provenance can be useful for various tasks: for example, to validate the execution as represented in the provenance record, to manage expectation failures, or to provide explanations.</rdfs:comment>
    <prov:component>agents-responsibility</prov:component>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#"/>
    <prov:definition>A plan is an entity that represents a set of actions or steps intended by one or more agents to achieve some goals.</prov:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://in2use.com/process_model/Goal">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://in2use.com/process_model/State_Description"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Goal</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://in2use.com/process_model"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Goal</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A state description specifying a condition to be achieved or maintained.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://in2use.com/process_model/Interval_Finishes_Direct_Dates">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#Imp"/>
    <swrl:body rdf:nodeID="Nea53287fca0444f188bbf5b74959a5a6"/>
    <swrl:head rdf:nodeID="Ndd22bd78dadc4f899e689613aa1d1cd2"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Interval Finishes Direct Dates</rdfs:label>
    <swrla:isRuleEnabled rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</swrla:isRuleEnabled>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen interval relation: b.start &lt; a.start and a.end = b.end. Compares time:inXSDDateTimeStamp values directly; both intervals must have beginning/end timestamps with start &lt; end. Equal timestamps may belong to distinct instant individuals. No instant-to-instant ordering is materialized. Inverse relations are supplied by the retained OWL-Time inverse-property axioms.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:altLabel>IntervalFinishes_DirectDates</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N1f33cb496f8e4d6ca94a25077b8d3d05">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="N55909e7289864edc9582cfa1b1db6f7b"/>
